    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1083">

                <pb facs="1010" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 351.622a/4</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 22, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6 p. m.</hi>] </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1171. Department’s 1248, December 13, 4 p. m. Minister for Foreign Affairs has,
                    just informed me the that of Marine up to to-day has not received sufficiently
                    detailed regarding in question to enable Foreign Office to reply but that the
                    captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Descartes</hi> was immediately asked for
                    the necessary information. Minister for Foreign Affairs adds that to acquaint me
                    with the result of this investigation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
